Z||000000||JohnnyK||07-04-2001||04:34 PM||||I don't understand it, it is the 15" that I'm supposed to have, but it is much to high for the sunroof to go over it.. Am i supposed to throw the spare in the trunk or something?||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||07-04-2001||04:46 PM||||Nooo, but how are you putting the panel in the front? Are you placing it on the rack, or are you just laying it on top of the tire at an angle? Forgive me if I'm getting remedial for ya, but many people aren't hip to how it goes in up there.<P>First, open the fronttrunk and take out the wind deflector. That's the curved blade thingy clipped in above the brake master cylinder parallel to the bottom of the windshield.<P>Then remove the sunroof panel. Obviously you know this part. Then put the front edge of the panel on the two little ledges <B>above</B> the spare. Lowering the backof th panel down onto the plastic piece thar the wind deflector was clipped to, slide the latch into the hole in the middle. Clip the deflector into the holes that held on to the front of the roof panel, close your hood and you are in business. Enjoy the nice weather! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||07-04-2001||05:30 PM||||You can fit a<I> Full Size 15" spare in there?!?!</I>  I thought it <I>had</I> to go in the back.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
